WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.668
Ukraine's potential membership

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.770
in NATO will also be top of mind

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.270
as President

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.638
Biden prepares to head overseas

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.507
for NATO's summit next week.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:08.475
CNN's Fareed Zakaria

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:09.609
just sat down

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:10.410
with President Biden

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.611
for an exclusive interview

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.413
and asked him about Ukraine

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:15.515
wanting to join NATO's very much.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.616
Take a listen.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.453
When you go to the NATO summit,

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:23.757
the big strategic issue is that Ukraine

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:27.093
wants membership in NATO

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.129
should it get membership NATO.

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:29.729
I don't think it's

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:30.964
ready for membership in NATO's.

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:32.532
But here's the deal.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.067
I spent,

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.101
as you know, a

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:35.902
great deal of time

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.270
trying to hold NATO's together

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.739
because I believe has had

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:40.940
an overwhelming objective

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:41.841
from the time we launched

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.843
285,000 troops in Ukraine.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.346
And that was to break Naito.

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:48.348
He was confident in my view,

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:49.749
and many in the intelligence community

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.851
he was company could break narrow

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.153
to holding there together

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:54.954
is really critical.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:56.756
I don't think there is unanimity

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:57.323
in NATO's

00:00:57.323 --> 00:01:01.027
about whether or not to bring Ukraine

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:04.597
into the NATO's family.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.533
Now, at this moment

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:07.734
in the middle of a war,

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:08.301
for example,

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:09.569
if you did that,

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.438
then, you know, we I

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:13.206
and I mean what I say,

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.140
we're determined

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:14.474
to commit

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:16.476
every inch of

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:18.611
territory that is NATO's territory.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.680
It's a commitment that we've all made,

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.115
no matter what.

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:23.183
If the war is going

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:25.919
on, then we're all in the war.

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.120
You know, we're at war with Russia,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.621
if that were the case.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.224
So I think we have to lay out a path

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:35.195
for a rational path for Russia, for

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:35.495
you and me,

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:36.262
for Ukraine

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:39.766
to be able to qualify to get into Naito.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.769
And we have when the very first time

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.104
I met with Putin

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.805
two years ago, in Geneva,

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:46.406
and he said,

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:49.175
I want commitments on no Ukraine

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:50.810
and NATO,

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:51.911
I said, we're not going to do that

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.280
because it's an open door policy.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.583
We're not going to shut anybody out.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.284
Naito is a process

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.419
that takes some time

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:01.488
to meet all the qualifications

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:03.256
and from democratization

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:05.358
to a whole range of other issues.

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:06.759
So in the meantime, though,

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:07.994
I've spoken with Zelensky

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:09.662
at length about this.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:12.165
And one of the things I indicated is

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:12.999
the United States

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.234
would be ready

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.135
to provide

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:17.237
while the process was going on.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.072
And it's going to take a while

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.039
while that process

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:22.475
is going on to provide security.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:23.810
All the security

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.845
we provide for you, for Israel,

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:26.946
providing the weaponry

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.681
that needs the capacity

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:30.016
to defend themselves.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.651
If there is an agreement,

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:32.819
if there is a cease fire,

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.621
if there is a peace agreement,

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:36.322
and so I think we can work it out.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.291
And but I think it's premature

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.360
to say to call for a vote,

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.995
you know, in now

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:44.597
because there's other qualifications

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:45.331
to be reminded

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.733
clearly in democratization

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:47.700
and some of those issues.

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:49.702
You can see

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:50.703
all of Fareed's interview

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:51.504
with President Biden

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.573
this Sunday on Jeeps.

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:54.841
That airs at 10 a.m.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.943
Eastern only on CNN.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:57.443
Joining us now

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.044
to discuss,

00:02:58.044 --> 00:02:59.412
a member of the House Foreign Affairs

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:00.180
Committee, New York

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.614
Republican Congressman Mike Lawlor.

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:02.649
Congressman, good to see you.

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:04.050
Thanks for joining us today.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:04.984
Republican Senator

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.920
Lindsey Graham for having me.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:09.055
Lindsey Graham implied he wants Ukraine's

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:11.090
native membership to happen right away.

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:11.658
Lindsey

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.226
Graham says he's trying to get both sides

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:13.960
of the aisle,

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.495
Democrats and Republicans in the Senate,

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:18.264
to sign on to a resolution to urge

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:21.834
Naito to accept Ukraine

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.903
Would you sign onto such a thing

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:26.906
if it came before you in the House?

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.542
Well, it's certainly something that

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:31.077
will be under consideration.

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:33.780
We had a hearing just a few weeks ago

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:36.082
with administration officials

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.717
specifically I

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:38.851
and some of my colleagues

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.353
asked about

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:42.855
Ukraine's acceptance into NAITO

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.757
and whether or not the administration

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.893
would be pushing for that.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:49.195
At the Naito Summit,

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:49.729
obviously,

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:52.198
we have our answer from the president.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.434
He does not think they are ready for it.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:57.503
I do think that the sooner

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:00.607
Ukraine joins Naito, the better.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.208
Obviously, there is a process.

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:03.810
It does take time.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.979
But I do think the administration

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:09.048
should be more forward leaning in pushing

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:12.418
for Ukraine's acceptance into naito.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:14.654
I think at the end of the day here,

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:17.090
the president is right

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:20.393
insofar as Russia and Vladimir Putin

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:21.794
certainly thought

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.096
that they could break naito,

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:25.198
that we would not be unified

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:27.333
with our allies in response

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.168
to their illegal war

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.204
and invasion of Ukraine.

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:32.538
We have been unified.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.707
We need to continue to be unified

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:36.676
and we need to ensure

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:37.810
that Ukraine

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.313
is able to defend its sovereignty.

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:42.015
And I have been very strong

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:43.683
in support of this

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:45.084
from the beginning

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:47.553
because Vladimir Putin is a vile thug

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:48.721
and dictator

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.089
and has no interest

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:51.591
in stopping at Ukraine.

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:52.959
And that much is clear.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:53.493
So, look,

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:56.496
let's talk about the cluster bomb News

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:57.830
today that the Biden

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.032
administration, Biden administration

00:04:59.032 --> 00:04:59.732
is going to provide

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.200
cluster bombs to Ukraine

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.902
even though the United States

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:05.004
has not banned cluster bombs.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:05.972
But the U.S.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:06.673
did begin

00:05:06.673 --> 00:05:08.775
phasing out the use of cluster bombs

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:10.143
about seven or eight years ago

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.611
because of the potential danger

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.645
they pose to civilians,

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:15.181
because so many do not go off immediately

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.783
and also because of the widespread

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:18.384
explosion radius.

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:19.686
And though the Pentagon insists

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:21.788
that the so-called dud rate is low,

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:25.458
they still do pose risks to civilians

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:26.959
Do you think it's a good idea

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:29.562
Look, I

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:31.064
think obviously, as the president

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:34.000
alluded to, you know, the Ukrainian

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.369
military is running low on ammunition.

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:39.505
You've in the last few weeks seen

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:43.276
a breakdown between Vladimir Putin

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:45.378
and the Wagner group.

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:45.845
And so

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:48.548
I think the counteroffensive is critical

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:50.950
And we're at a critical stage

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.151
in this war

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:53.553
and for Ukraine's ability

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:54.620
to defend itself.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:55.621
And so I think

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:58.191
getting them as much ammunition

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:00.860
and weaponry as possible

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:02.462
is critically important.

00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:05.098
I think there's two key points to note.

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:06.165
Number one, obviously,

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:09.635
we are not party to any any agreement

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:12.071
on the use of cluster munitions.

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:14.040
But in addition to that,

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:14.974
these would be used

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:17.877
by Ukraine in defense of its sovereignty.

00:06:18.578 --> 00:06:21.414
In its own borders as opposed to,

00:06:22.115 --> 00:06:24.951
you know, bombing outside of its borders.

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:26.786
And I think that is a distinction

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:28.354
that is important to note.

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:29.122
They are trying

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:31.290
to defend their sovereignty

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.126
and they are at war

00:06:33.126 --> 00:06:33.993
with Russia

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:36.462
and the Russian military and its forces.

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:40.299
So I think in this instance, given what

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:42.668
the use is intended for,

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:44.170
given the limited

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:46.873
chance of

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:50.443
it impacting civilian casualties,

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:53.980
I do think it is the right decision.

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:55.581
And I think

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:56.516
and I support

00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:57.450
what the administration

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:58.551
is trying to do here.

00:06:58.551 --> 00:06:58.885
All right.

00:06:58.885 --> 00:06:59.886
Republican congressman

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:01.187
from New York, Mike Lawlor.

00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:02.155
Thank you so much, sir.

00:07:02.155 --> 00:07:02.922
Have a good weekend.

